  "body": "## Why\nA production CATALOG_SCAN could find several good listings but start only one negotiation. Older DISCOVERED listings were then considered again only if they still appeared in the current newest-first catalog page, so valid offers could fall out of the page and remain stranded forever.\n\nThe latest runtime log also exposed a target-matcher false negative: `Samsung Galaxy S25 SM-S931 12/128GB Enterprise Edition Srebrny` was rejected as if `S931` were a competing Samsung model, even though it is a manufacturer product code.\n\n## What changed\n- process the full persisted DISCOVERED backlog instead of intersecting it away with only the current scan\n- preserve newest-first priority while guaranteeing backlog progress with a 3-fresh : 2-backlog ordering\n- keep backlog oldest-first so it drains deterministically\n- continue to apply price guard, target checks, mandatory full-title verification, availability/offer-action checks, persistent FIRST_OFFER guard and quota before submit\n- allow several confirmed first offers in one production CATALOG_SCAN instead of returning after the first success\n- continue past candidate-local failures that happen strictly before guard/quota/submit; guard refusal and ambiguous post-quota failures still fail closed\n- add production throughput env vars:\n  - `FLIPBOT_MAX_REAL_OFFERS_PER_CATALOG_SCAN` default 3, range 1..5\n  - `FLIPBOT_MAX_REAL_NEXT_STEPS_PER_CHECK` default 1, range 1..5\n- controlled mode remains hard-capped at one action regardless of those env vars\n- fix Samsung `SM-Sxxx` technical product codes so they do not conflict with marketing model keys such as `S25`, while still rejecting S24, S25 Ultra, etc.\n- update runtime logging/docs\n\n## Tests added\n- backlog/current-scan fairness and empty-current-scan backlog draining\n- Samsung S25/S25+/S24/Ultra matcher regressions\n- production vs controlled action-limit behavior and limit parsing\n\n## Preserved safety invariant\nThe backend's current global marketplace `listingId` claim remains unchanged, so multiple bot accounts still cannot independently claim the same Vinted listing.",
